<!--
  PCoin miner launcher foreground: a struck coin.

  GENERATED. Do not hand-edit. Regenerate from contrib/branding/make-icons.ps1,
  which emits this file, the SVG the website uses, every PNG and the Windows
  .ico from one set of constants. Editing here silently desyncs the platforms.

  108x108 is the adaptive viewport; a launcher shows only the middle 72x72 and
  only the central 66x66 circle survives every OEM mask, so the whole mark sits
  inside that circle.

  The shapes are CUT, not overpainted: the star is a hole in the face and the
  lettering is a hole in the base, both via evenOdd. That keeps the foreground
  genuinely transparent there, which is what makes the Android 13 monochrome
  layer render as a coin rather than a solid blob.
-->
